WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:01.720
A family story.

2
00:00:01.720 --> 00:00:04.240
A grandmother wrote home every Sunday,

3
00:00:04.240 --> 00:00:06.800
and her sister kept every letter:

4
00:00:06.800 --> 00:00:10.100
«Ces lettres, sa sœur les a toutes
gardées.» Now something simpler.

5
00:00:10.100 --> 00:00:13.030
«J'ai pris les photos.» Then:

6
00:00:13.030 --> 00:00:13.920
«Ces photos ?

7
00:00:13.920 --> 00:00:16.220
Je les ai prises.» Listen again.

8
00:00:16.220 --> 00:00:18.840
A new sound appears at
the end of the verb.

9
00:00:18.840 --> 00:00:21.170
Same verb, same photos.

10
00:00:21.170 --> 00:00:22.430
So why do the spelling,

11
00:00:22.430 --> 00:00:24.920
and even the sound, change?

12
00:00:24.920 --> 00:00:30.430
In this mission, you'll split events from
background on Mission D1's two-camera timeline.

13
00:00:30.430 --> 00:00:33.480
Then you'll flip the switches
in Mission I1 and watch

14
00:00:33.480 --> 00:00:35.630
what happens to «écrit».

15
00:00:35.630 --> 00:00:39.580
Your mission: find out why the
same verb is written two ways,

16
00:00:39.580 --> 00:00:40.830
and when it changes.
